[{"id":4889430066,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI27IMg","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"8815a5d1232a80efbb0ca4af30cb9f044bc71514","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","login":"lyuma","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma"},"body":"Approved in meeting\n\nI found that the option does not work if relative is false (still the default, for compatibility reasons). Hide `use_rest_for_limitation` if `relative` is false. For relative=false, the current behavior is intended since the modifier already has the behavior of use rest pose for limitation, since the calculations are done relative to the rest pose. Just a simple change to hide the checkbox in this case should be enough.\n\nIt took me a while to find the correct combination of settings. In the future, it would be helpful to have a gizmo that shows the limitation axes, and also a flat disc for `use_secondary_rotation=false`.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121394#pullrequestreview-4889430066","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121394","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-08-08T18:36:01Z"},{"id":4890800442,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI4OxOg","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"d538d97dc319ae38fb0d2ebc443c5614c15bb5f5","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","login":"lyuma","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"publi